From: RetroPixel Pocket bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip-inno-usb2: skip rppocket power-on reset

The working RetroPixel Pocket stock 4.4 USB2PHY driver clears phy_sus and then
waits for UTMI clock stability. Mainline 6.12 additionally resets the PHY
after clearing phy_sus. On this board, ROCKNIX reaches DWC2 host mode and
powers the port, but HPRT0 never observes linestate/connect while stock does.

Test the remaining stock/mainline delta by skipping the post-power-on USB2PHY
reset only for the FunnyPlaying RetroPixel Pocket.

---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -628,7 +628,14 @@ static int rockchip_usb2phy_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 	 * please keep the common_on_n 1'b0 to set these blocks
 	 * remain powered.
 	 */
-	ret = rockchip_usb2phy_reset(rphy);
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("funnyplaying,rppocket")) {
+		dev_info(rphy->dev,
+			 "RPPDBG usb2phy skip power-on reset for rppocket port=%u\n",
+			 rport->port_id);
+		ret = 0;
+	} else {
+		ret = rockchip_usb2phy_reset(rphy);
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
